ew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: Anticipate dangerous situations (good decision quality), see complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), leadership qualities (crew cooperation, responsibility). Concerns: show-off (could affect crew cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability). No explicit stress resilience or reliability info.\n\nB: Very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), weak memory for numbers (attention accuracy), makes nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication). So strong reliability and stress but poor teamwork.\n\nC: Makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality), keeps calm in crisis (stress), understands complicated technology (technical), difficulty communicating ideas (crew cooperation), egocentric (crew), not willing to further education (adaptability). So good decision and stress but poor communication.\n\nD: Responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), know-it-all (crew cooperation), hot temper (crew). So mixed.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate B has strong reliability and stress but poor teamwork. C has good decision and stress but poor communication. A has strong technical and leadership but show-off and not open. D has good problem solving but hot temper.\n\nWhich candidate balances? Maybe none perfect. Need to weigh. The panel should discuss all. As first contribution, we can propose a candidate and give reasoning, maybe Candidate B for reliability and stress, but note concerns about teamwork. Or propose Candidate C for decision and calmness but note communication issues. Which is stronger? Reliability is crucial; B is very conscientious, which is key. However nasty remarks are serious for crew cooperation. That may be disqualifying. C's communication difficulty also serious. A's show-off may be less severe? Not open to new ideas also concerning for adaptability. D's hot temper also serious.\n\nThus maybe B is still best despite remarks? Need to decide. As first contribution, we can state provisional recommendation for Candidate B, citing strengths, and note concerns to be addressed later. That aligns with starting discussion.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I would currently recommend Candidate B because ...\". Include facts. Then metadata vote B."}
